export const MODEL_KB = "## What DeepWell is [article_id: what-is-deepwell]\nDeepWell is a hosted records system for any business that stores documents or paperwork. It reads your invoices, work orders, contracts, forms and photos of documents, links them to the right customer and address, and lets the team ask questions in plain language. Every answer shows its source. Equipment paperwork such as warranties, serial numbers and service tickets is where it understands the most today.\nQ: What is DeepWell?\nA: DeepWell finds the answer in your own records. Your invoices, work orders, contracts, forms and photos of documents go in, DeepWell reads them and links each fact to the right customer and address (and, for equipment paperwork, the right unit), and your team asks questions the way they would ask a coworker. Every answer shows the source document. We set it up for you, so day one is already useful.\nQ: Who is DeepWell for?\nA: DeepWell is for any small or mid-sized business that stores documents or paperwork, from an owner-operator to a multi-team company. Equipment paperwork such as warranties, serial numbers and service tickets is where it is deepest today. Office staff use it to answer callers, people in the field use it on a phone, and owners use it to see expiring warranties and agreements.\nQ: Do you support electrical, plumbing or property management?, electrical contractors, just hvac, only hvac\nA: You can upload electrical, plumbing or property-management paperwork today, because DeepWell reads any business documents. What is not live yet are the industry-specific features, such as backflow-test tracking or lease handling. Those pages are on the site and marked coming soon, with no dates. You can join the waitlist from those pages or email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Will DeepWell work for my business?\nA: If your business keeps documents or paperwork, yes. DeepWell reads invoices, contracts, permits, forms, correspondence and photos of documents, files them by customer and address, and answers questions with the original page attached. Equipment paperwork (warranties, serials, service tickets) is where it understands the most today. It does not have industry-specific features for other fields yet, and I can't promise dates for them. Not sure? Send one sample box free and see the result before you commit.\nQ: How does DeepWell work?\nA: Three steps. **Ingest:** paper, PDFs, Word and Excel files, CSVs and photos go in as they are. **Link:** each document is read for serials, addresses, dates, names and amounts, and connected to the matching customer and equipment. **Ask:** you type a question and get the answer with the source page attached. Uncertain reads are flagged for a quick human check.\nQ: What kinds of records can DeepWell read?\nA: Invoices, work orders, contracts and agreements, permits, forms, purchase orders, inspection reports, correspondence and photos of documents, plus warranty cards, startup sheets, service tickets and nameplate photos. DeepWell reads handwritten and low-quality scans too. Nothing has to be renamed or filed first.\nQ: Who are the founders?\nA: DeepWell was founded by two brothers. **Hilton Chapman** is a retired Air Force veteran who leads customer relationships and marketing and sets the vision. **Sterling Chapman** has prior Army service and is the engineer behind the platform. He works with you from your first sample through go-live.\nQ: Where is DeepWell based?\nA: DeepWell Technology LLC is based in Alamogordo, New Mexico, USA.\nQ: Is there a free demo or sample?\nA: Yes. Send one sample box or folder of old invoices, tickets or warranties and we will digitize it free so you can see the result before you commit to the rest. Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com to start. Solo also has a 30-day free trial.\nQ: What is white-glove setup?\nA: Every plan includes setup by our team. We inventory your records, run the first bulk ingest, check the links against the questions your office actually asks, and train your crew in an afternoon.\n\n## Signing in, logins and roles [article_id: signing-in-and-logins]\nPeople sign in with their own DeepWell account. A company is one account, and the owner invites everyone else from the Team screen.\nQ: How many logins does my plan include?\nA: Solo includes up to 2 logins, Team up to 5, Crew up to 10, and Fleet 11+. The owner account is not counted. So a Team plan can have the owner plus five more people.\nQ: Is the owner counted as a login?\nA: No. The owner account does not count toward the login limit on any plan.\nQ: How do I invite a team member?\nA: An admin opens **Team** (people icon in the top bar), then **Invite someone**: type the email, pick **Member** or **Admin**, and press **Send invite**. They accept from the email and land in your company, on the computer or the phone app. Invites count toward your plan's login limit. Team is desktop only.\nQ: What are the roles, admin and member?\nA: Two roles. **Admins** can manage billing and API keys, invite and remove people, export or delete the company's data, delete documents, merge duplicate customers, send outreach and grant support access. **Members** can ask Donovan, upload and scan, browse, fix and verify records. A member sees those admin buttons greyed out with \"Ask an admin\" next to them (Export CSV, customer merge, Billing buttons, API keys), and the delete buttons are hidden for them, so ask an admin to do it.\nQ: Can I go over my login limit?\nA: The invite form is disabled once you reach your plan's limit: \"Your plan's login limit is reached — upgrade to invite more people,\" with a **Go to Billing** link. If you're over the limit nobody is locked out, but new invites pause until you're under it or upgrade. Pending invites count. Fleet has no DeepWell login cap.\nQ: How do I sign in or reset my password?\nA: Desktop: go to deepwelltechnology.com/app (or choose **Log in** on the website). Phone: open the DeepWell app on your home screen, or deepwelltechnology.com/m. Forgot your password? Use the password option (the forgot password link) on the sign-in form. If you are still locked out, email support@deepwelltechnology.com from the address on your account. Never send a password in chat or email.\nQ: How do I sign out?\nA: Desktop: **Sign out** is at the far right of the top bar. Phone: tap the round profile button (your initial) at the top right to open the **Account** sheet, then tap **Sign out**. If scans are still waiting to upload, the phone warns you first that signing out deletes them from the phone; choose **Stay signed in** to keep them, or **Sign out and delete**.\nQ: How do I switch to a different company?\nA: If you belong to more than one company, use the company switcher in the desktop top bar (next to **Sign out**). The app reloads on that company's records. On the phone, tap the round profile button at the top right to open the **Account** sheet; when you belong to more than one company it lists them under **Switch company**. Switching reloads the app on the other company. Scans still waiting to upload stay with the company they were taken in and only upload when that company is active again.\nQ: I just signed in and it asks me to create or join a company. What do I do?\nA: An account belongs to a company. If you're the owner, choose **Create your company** and name it, and you become its admin. If someone invited you, choose **I was invited** (or open the link in your invite email) and accept, using the same email address the invite went to. The phone app says \"Join your company first\" until you have one.\nQ: How do I change someone's role?\nA: An admin opens **Team** and uses the **Members** tab of the panel under the invite form (it's our sign-in provider's panel). Change the person's role between **Member** and **Admin** on their row. Admins can manage billing, invites, exports, deletion and support access, so keep Admin for people who need it. Only admins can change roles.\nQ: How do I remove a user or team member who left?\nA: An admin opens **Team**, finds the person on the **Members** tab of the panel under the invite form (our sign-in provider's panel), and removes them from their row's menu. Their access ends and the login is freed up. The company's records stay with the company. Only admins can remove people.\nQ: Can I cancel or resend an invite?\nA: Pending invites show in the **Team** header as \"N pending invites\" and on the **Invitations** tab of the panel below the invite form. Revoke one there, then send a new one from **Invite someone** if the address was wrong. A pending invite uses a login until it is accepted or revoked.\nQ: How do I see how many logins I've used?\nA: On **Team**, the pill at the top right reads like \"3 of 5 logins used (owner not counted)\" and adds \"N pending invites\". **Billing** shows your plan's login limit. Members only see a member count.\nQ: Does DeepWell charge per team member?\nA: No. Plans are priced by team size tier, not per team member. Each plan has a set number of logins, a storage limit and a monthly scan allowance.\n\n## Plans and pricing [article_id: plans-and-pricing]\nFour plans: Solo, Team, Crew and Fleet. All prices are in US dollars. Donovan, our question-answering assistant, is unlimited on every plan.\nQ: How much does DeepWell cost?\nA: Solo is $99/month, Team $199/month, Crew $399/month and Fleet $899+/month. Every plan includes unlimited Donovan, white-glove setup and data export. Plans differ by logins, storage, monthly scan volume and support. Full details are on the Pricing section of deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What does the Solo plan include?\nA: **Solo, $99/month**, for the owner-operator: up to 2 logins, 25,000 documents stored, 750 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, email support with a next-business-day response, and a 30-day free trial (card required).\nQ: What does the Team plan include?\nA: **Team, $199/month** (formerly Shop), for a small company: up to 5 logins, 100,000 documents stored, 2,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, and email plus chat support with a same-business-day response.\nQ: What does the Crew plan include?\nA: **Crew, $399/month**, for a growing crew: up to 10 logins, 500,000 documents stored, 5,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, email, chat and phone support with a 2-hour response for urgent issues, and a scheduled onboarding call.\nQ: What does the Fleet plan include?\nA: **Fleet, $899+/month**, for multi-crew teams: 11+ logins, unlimited documents stored, 10,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, API access, a named contact (Sterling) from first sample to go-live, and a 1-hour response for urgent issues, 24/7. For Fleet pricing beyond the base, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What is included in every plan?\nA: Every plan includes unlimited Donovan with sources, white-glove setup by our team, and the ability to export your data anytime. A public status page is live at status.deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is there annual pricing or a discount?\nA: Yes. Pay annually and you get one month free, so a year costs 11 times the monthly price: Solo $1,089, Team $2,189, Crew $4,389 and Fleet $9,889. I can't offer other discounts or custom terms. For those, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is DeepWell priced per team member?\nA: No. Pricing is by plan tier, not per team member. Pick the plan that fits your team size, scan volume and support needs.\nQ: Which plan should I choose?\nA: Match the plan to your team. **Solo** fits an owner-operator with up to 2 logins. **Team** fits up to 5 logins. **Crew** fits up to 10. **Fleet** is for 11 or more logins or if you need API access. The owner account is not counted. Scan allowance grows with each plan: 750, 2,000, 5,000 and 10,000 pages a month.\nQ: Is Donovan really unlimited?\nA: Yes. Donovan is unlimited on every plan. There is a fair-use safety limit that ordinary use never reaches. It exists only to stop runaway automation.\nQ: Are there setup fees or contracts?\nA: Setup by our team is included with every plan, and I don't see a separate setup fee listed. Monthly plans can be canceled at any time. Annual prepay locks in the annual price. Records Rescue scanning is a separate paid service.\n\n## Free trial and billing states [article_id: trial-and-billing-dates]\nThe free trial is on Solo only. Billing has four states: trialing, active, past due and canceled.\nQ: Is there a free trial?\nA: Yes. Solo has a **30-day free trial**. A card is required, you won't be charged until the trial ends, and you can cancel anytime. Team, Crew and Fleet do not have a trial. If you want to see DeepWell on your own records first, ask about the free sample box.\nQ: Do I need a credit card for the trial?\nA: Yes, a card is required at checkout for the Solo trial. You won't be charged until the 30 days are over, and you can cancel before then.\nQ: Can I get a second free trial?\nA: The free trial is one per account. Canceling and signing up again does not start a new one. For an extension request, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What happens if my payment fails?\nA: You keep full access for a **7-day grace period** after the due date. After that, uploads pause, but you can still read and ask Donovan about your existing records. Update your card from **Billing → Manage billing** (admins only) to restore full access.\nQ: What happens when I cancel?\nA: Cancellation on a monthly plan takes effect at the end of the current billing period. Once a subscription has ended, you'll be asked to choose a plan to keep uploading and asking questions. You can export your data first; see the export article.\nQ: Where can I see my renewal or trial end date?\nA: Open **Billing** in the app. It shows your plan, status, trial end or renewal date and this month's usage. Admins can also open **Manage billing** for invoices and payment methods. If you ask me while signed in, I can look up your plan and dates.\nQ: What does \"Choose a plan to get started\" mean?\nA: Your account has no active plan, either because you haven't subscribed yet or the subscription has ended. Open **Billing** and pick a plan. Until then only Billing and Team are available.\n\n## Add-ons and Records Rescue [article_id: add-ons]\nThree things are sold on top of a plan: Records Rescue scanning, the automatic outreach add-on, and API access, which comes with Fleet.\nQ: What is Records Rescue?\nA: Records Rescue is our scanning service for old paper. Full service is **$0.12 per page with a $500 minimum**. It is billed separately from your plan and can be bought under Billing. It is non-refundable once scanning has begun. You can start with a free sample box first.\nQ: Can I try Records Rescue before paying?\nA: Yes. Send one sample folder or box of old invoices, tickets or warranties and we digitize it free so you can see the result before committing to the rest. Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com to arrange it.\nQ: What is the automatic outreach add-on?\nA: DeepWell can draft warranty-upsell emails to your customers when a unit's warranty is about to end. In review mode a person approves and sends each one, and that needs no add-on. The fully automatic, unattended sending is a paid add-on. For its price, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is API access an add-on?\nA: API access is included on the **Fleet** plan only. Fleet admins create and revoke API keys in the app. Other plans can't create keys. Ready-made integrations with other software are not listed as available today.\nQ: Does DeepWell integrate with QuickBooks or other software?\nA: No built-in integrations are listed as available today. Google Drive sync and email or folder intake are marked coming soon, with no date. You can export CSV for dispatch and accounting, and Fleet has API access.\n\n## Changing or canceling a plan, invoices, refunds [article_id: change-cancel-plan-invoices]\nPlan changes, cards and invoices are handled in Billing, through Stripe's billing portal. Only company admins can open it.\nQ: How do I upgrade or change my plan?\nA: An admin opens **Billing → Choose a plan**, picks **Monthly** or **Annual · 1 month free**, then presses **Choose plan** on the tier they want. Your current tier shows **Current plan**. Payment happens on Stripe's secure checkout page. Members can open Billing but can't change the plan. Not sure which plan fits? Ask me or email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: How do I cancel my subscription?\nA: An admin opens **Billing → Manage billing** (in the Current plan card), which opens Stripe's billing portal, and cancels there. A monthly plan can be canceled any time and takes effect at the end of the current billing period, and Billing then shows \"Ends <date>\". There are no prorated refunds for partial months. Want a person to handle it? I can send your request to the team.\nQ: What is your refund policy?\nA: Monthly plans are not refunded for partial months. Annual plans are refundable in full if you cancel within 30 days of the first annual payment, and non-refundable after that. Records Rescue is non-refundable once scanning has begun. If you believe you were billed in error, contact us within 30 days of the charge at support@deepwelltechnology.com. I can't issue refunds myself.\nQ: Where do I find my invoices or receipts?\nA: An admin opens **Billing → Manage billing**. Stripe's portal lists every invoice and receipt to view or download. Members can't open the portal. If one is missing, email billing@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: How do I update my credit card?\nA: An admin opens **Billing → Manage billing** and updates the payment method in Stripe's portal. Card details are handled by Stripe; DeepWell never sees or stores your card number. Please don't type a card number into this chat.\nQ: Does DeepWell store my credit card?\nA: No. Stripe, our payment processor, handles and stores your card details and processes payments directly. DeepWell stores your subscription and billing status and a Stripe customer ID, never your card number. Please don't type a card number into this chat.\nQ: Do you offer refunds for the free trial?\nA: You aren't charged during the 30-day Solo trial (a card is required to start), and you can cancel any time before it ends. If you were charged and believe it was a mistake, contact us within 30 days of the charge at support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## Uploading and scanning on the web app [article_id: uploading-and-scanning-web]\nRecords go in through the Inbox in the web app, or through Scan in the phone app. Nothing has to be renamed or filed first.\nQ: How do I upload documents?\nA: Open **Inbox**, stay on the **Add files** tab and press **Add files** (top right), or drag files onto **Bulk import**. DeepWell wraps each drop in a batch; **New batch** lets you name one (Name, Source such as Filing cabinet, Email, Shared drive or Truck, and From/To dates). A brand-new company lands here with \"Add your first document.\" Nothing needs renaming or filing first. On a phone use the **Scan** tab instead.\nQ: What file types can I upload?\nA: On the desktop **Inbox → Add files → Bulk import** takes **Choose files or a .zip**, or drag a .zip or folder in. Accepted: .zip .pdf .jpg .jpeg .png .gif .webp .txt .md .csv .tsv .json .docx .xlsx (iPhone .heic/.heif photos are converted to JPEG automatically in Safari). It skips folders, hidden files, macOS archive metadata, empty files, unsupported types and files that are too large, and shows counts like \"12 files · 9 uploaded · 3 skipped\". A .zip inside a .zip is not opened, and a .zip that expands to far more than it should is refused. **Cancel** stops a run. Old Word and Excel files (.doc, .xls), files with macros (.docm, .xlsm, .xlsb) and password-protected files are not read: open them and Save As .docx or .xlsx (or PDF) first.\nQ: Is there a file size limit?\nA: PDFs and photos must be under 24 MB, text, CSV, Word and Excel files under 20 MB, and 100 MB is the hard ceiling. Up to 50 files go in per upload request (bulk import sends them in groups). Your plan also has a monthly page allowance and there is a daily upload limit that resets at UTC midnight. For a bigger PDF, split it into smaller files first.\nQ: Why wasn't my Word or Excel file read?\nA: DeepWell reads Word (.docx) and Excel (.xlsx) files: the text and tables of a Word file and every sheet of an Excel file. Formulas show the value that was last saved in the file. Pictures inside a Word file (including a scanned page pasted in as an image), and charts or pictures in a spreadsheet, are not read, so save or scan that page as a PDF or photo instead. Old .doc and .xls files, files that can contain macros (.docm, .xlsm, .xlsb) and password-protected files are not read: open the file, use Save As to make a plain .docx or .xlsx (remove the password first), then upload that copy. A file renamed to .docx that isn't really a Word file is refused.\nQ: What happens to iPhone photos?\nA: An iPhone saves photos as HEIC by default. DeepWell converts them to JPEG automatically, on the device, in Safari on iPhone and iPad (and Safari on a Mac), then uploads the JPEG. Other browsers often can't open HEIC; if you see a message saying the photo can't be converted, set the iPhone camera to Settings > Camera > Formats > Most Compatible, or share or export the photo as a JPEG, and add it again. DeepWell never receives the raw HEIC file.\nQ: How long until an upload is searchable?\nA: Usually within minutes. Each file shows Checking, Uploading, Reading or Queued while it goes in, then a stage pill: **Uploaded → Sorted → Read → Matched → Checked** (or **AI verified**). The header shows \"Processing N of M…\", or \"Still working on N — check Inbox\" after ten minutes. Watch it in **Inbox**; the bell tells you about later changes. A file that is accepted but not finished shows \"Still processing — check Inbox in a few minutes\" with a **See Needs you** button. Big batches take longer.\nQ: What does the Classify received button do?\nA: On **Inbox → Add files**, a batch with files still at **Uploaded** shows **Classify received**. Press it and DeepWell works out what kind of document each file is, the same way it does for the rest of your records. It never overwrites a type a person chose. It then reports \"Classified N of M.\" If some could not be placed it says the rest need a person: open them under **Inbox → Needs you** and pick the document type. If a file is still uploading, wait a moment and press it again.\nQ: Can DeepWell read handwriting and bad scans?\nA: Yes. DeepWell reads handwriting, carbon copies and low-quality scans. When a read is uncertain it flags the document for a quick human check instead of guessing.\nQ: Can I forward emails or sync a folder?\nA: Email intake and folder sync are marked **coming soon** and are not available today, and I can't give a date. For now, upload files in Inbox or use the phone app to scan. For a big backlog, our team runs the first bulk ingest during setup.\nQ: Can my whole backlog of paper be scanned for me?\nA: Yes. White-glove setup includes a first bulk ingest, and Records Rescue can scan paper for you at $0.12 per page with a $500 minimum. Start with a free sample box.\nQ: What if I upload the same file twice?\nA: DeepWell recognizes a file by its contents. A second copy shows \"Already on file (matched by content)\" and no duplicate is created, even if the file name is different.\n\n## The phone app and how to install it [article_id: mobile-app-and-install]\nDeepWell Mobile installs from your browser. There is nothing to download from an app store and nothing to update.\nQ: Is there a DeepWell phone app?\nA: Yes. DeepWell Mobile works on iPhone, iPad and Android. It has three tabs: **Ask** for Donovan, **Scan** for photographing paperwork and **Docs** for finding documents. The full desktop app has everything else: Inbox, Records, Dashboard, Team and Billing.\nQ: How do I install the app on iPhone?\nA: Open **deepwelltechnology.com/m** in **Safari**. Tap **Share**, scroll down, tap **Add to Home Screen**, then **Add**. Open DeepWell from your home screen and sign in there. The home-screen app keeps its own sign-in.\nQ: How do I install the app on Android?\nA: Open **deepwelltechnology.com/m** in **Chrome**. Tap **Install** when DeepWell offers it, or open the menu and choose **Install app** or **Add to Home screen**. Then open DeepWell from your home screen and sign in.\nQ: Why isn't it in the App Store or Google Play?\nA: It installs straight from the browser, so everyone always has the latest version. It gets its own icon and opens full screen like any other app. There's no store listing, so search the store won't find it. Use the install steps above.\nQ: Does the phone app cost extra?\nA: No. The phone app is included with every plan. Your team members sign in with their own DeepWell accounts, which the company owner invites from Team.\nQ: Does it work with bad signal?\nA: It is built for weak signal: it opens quickly, photos are shrunk on the phone before uploading, and slow answers show a retry. The app itself opens from the phone with weak or no signal. Asking Donovan needs a connection. A scan taken with no signal is saved on the phone and uploads by itself when the signal returns (see Waiting to upload on the Scan tab).\nQ: The install button doesn't show up. What do I do?\nA: Open the page in **Safari** on iPhone or **Chrome** on Android. In-app browsers such as those inside social, email or messaging apps can't install DeepWell. Use the menu there and choose **Open in Safari** or **Open in Chrome**, then try again.\nQ: How do I scan paperwork with my phone?\nA: Open the **Scan** tab and tap **Take photo** (rear camera), then **Add another page** if needed, or **Choose photos or PDFs**. With several photos, choose **One document, N pages** or **N separate documents**, then tap **Upload N pages**. DeepWell reads and files it, then shows \"Uploaded and read\". Then **Scan another** or **View docs**.\n\n## Scan status and the needs-info queue [article_id: scan-status-and-needs-info]\nEvery document moves through five stages. When DeepWell is unsure about something it asks you a short question instead of guessing.\nQ: What do the document stages mean?\nA: **Uploaded:** the file arrived. **Sorted:** DeepWell worked out what kind of document it is. **Read:** the text was read and facts such as serials, dates and amounts pulled out. **Matched:** the document was connected to the right customer and equipment. **Checked:** every required fact is present and confident, or a person confirmed it (an **AI verified** badge means DeepWell's own re-check passed).\nQ: My document is stuck or still processing. What should I do?\nA: Give it a few minutes; large files and batches take longer. Check **Inbox** after a refresh. If a document has sat at **Uploaded** for more than about 15 minutes, email support@deepwelltechnology.com with the file name and the time you uploaded it. Files that were accepted but not finished show \"Still processing — check Inbox in a few minutes\" with a **See Needs you** button that opens **Inbox → Needs you**, where anything that needs a person lands.\nQ: Why was my document flagged?\nA: DeepWell flags a document when a required fact is missing or unclear, for example a smudged nameplate or two possible customers. Open **Inbox → Needs you**, open the document, confirm or fix the value, and it moves on to **Checked**.\n\n## Monthly page allowance and storage limits [article_id: page-allowance-and-limits]\nEach plan has a monthly allowance of new pages, a documents-stored limit and a login limit. Donovan questions are not limited.\nQ: How many pages can I scan per month?\nA: Solo: 750 new pages a month. Team: 2,000. Crew: 5,000. Fleet: 10,000. A page is one page of a document: for a PDF, one printed page; a photo is one page. A Word (.docx) file counts about one page for every 3,000 characters of text (about one printed page), at least one. An Excel (.xlsx) or CSV file counts one page for each block of roughly 6,000 characters of a sheet (the header row is repeated in every block), and every sheet that has anything in it counts at least one; an empty sheet counts none. Plain text, Markdown and JSON count one page for every 6,000 characters. Signed in, ask me and I'll check your usage.\nQ: How are pages counted for Word, Excel and CSV files?\nA: A Word (.docx) file counts about one page per 3,000 characters of text, at least one. An Excel (.xlsx) or CSV file counts one page per block of roughly 6,000 characters of a sheet (header row repeated in each block); an empty sheet counts none. The real count is set when the file is read. Before that DeepWell uses a size estimate, which errs high for files full of pictures (not read or counted) and can be much lower for very repetitive files. The final count is checked at reading: a file that would use more pages than you have left this month is not added and nothing is counted. Only the final count is added to your monthly pages.\nQ: How many documents can I store?\nA: Solo stores up to 25,000 documents, Team 100,000, Crew 500,000, and Fleet is unlimited.\nQ: What happens when I reach my page limit?\nA: New uploads pause with a message that the monthly page limit is reached. Existing records and Donovan keep working. Upgrade your plan for a larger allowance, or email support@deepwelltechnology.com. If you have a large backlog, Records Rescue can scan it separately.\nQ: Do questions to Donovan count against my allowance?\nA: No. Donovan is unlimited on every plan. Only new pages you scan or upload count toward the monthly page allowance.\nQ: What does \"Donovan is seeing unusually high usage\" mean?\nA: It is the fair-use safety limit, which exists to stop runaway scripts. Ordinary use doesn't reach it. Email support@deepwelltechnology.com and we'll sort it out.\n\n## Using Donovan and reading sources [article_id: using-donovan-and-sources]\nDonovan is the DeepWell assistant that answers questions from your own records. This support chat explains how DeepWell works. Questions about your customers, equipment or jobs belong in Donovan.\nQ: What is Donovan?\nA: Donovan answers questions in plain language using your uploaded records: who a document is for, what an invoice totals, what a permit or agreement says, and, for equipment paperwork, warranty status, last service, model and serial. Every answer shows the source document, and if Donovan isn't sure it says so and shows the document instead of guessing.\nQ: How do I ask Donovan a question?\nA: Open **Ask** in the app, on desktop or in the phone app, and type the question the way you would ask a coworker, for example an address, a serial number, a name or a date. You get the answer with the source attached.\nQ: What kinds of questions can Donovan answer?\nA: Things like \"What did we pay Acme Supply in March?\", \"Show me the signed permit for 12 Main\" or \"When did we last service the unit at 3247 Elm?\" For equipment paperwork it also covers warranty status, model and serial numbers, and which units are expiring soon. It answers from your own records only, and says so when something isn't on file.\nQ: Can Donovan be wrong?\nA: Yes, AI answers can be incomplete or wrong. A misread serial, an old scan or a document that was never uploaded can all cause it. That's why every answer cites its source. Check the cited document before relying on an answer for a warranty claim, a safety decision or anything with financial consequences.\nQ: Why did Donovan say it couldn't find something?\nA: Usually the document hasn't been uploaded or finished processing, or the name, address or serial was read differently. Try the address or serial number, check the document's status in Inbox, and correct any flagged fields. If Donovan still misses something it should have found, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Can this chat look up my customer records?\nA: No. This chat only answers questions about DeepWell itself. For anything about your own customers, equipment, jobs or documents, ask **Donovan** in the app.\nQ: Does Donovan learn from my data or other customers' data?\nA: Your records stay under your own account and are never pooled with another company's. Under our AI providers' API terms your content isn't used to train their models. Your corrections make the system sharper. See the security article for details.\n\n## Exporting your data and reports [article_id: exports-and-warranty-export]\nYour data is yours. You can take a copy at any time.\nQ: Can I export my data?\nA: Yes, any time. An admin opens **Team → Settings → Your data** and presses **Download data export (JSON)**. It includes documents, page text, extractions, customer and unit records, links and audit log entries. Exporting is admin only and is recorded in your audit log.\nQ: Can I get my original files back?\nA: Yes, one at a time. Press **Open original** on a document (or **Download <file name>** in its preview) for a short-lived secure link. The data export lists every original with its file name, size and checksum. Bundling all originals into one zip is not built yet.\nQ: Can I export to CSV for dispatch or accounting?\nA: Yes. **Records → Documents → Export CSV** and **Records → Customers → Export CSV** (both admin only: a member sees the button greyed out with \"Ask an admin\" beside it), and **Records → Grid → Export CSV (N rows)**, which downloads the rows on screen and lets you pick columns first. For anything larger, such as a bulk API pull, Fleet has API access.\nQ: What is the warranty export?\nA: The warranty list lives on the **Dashboard**: the warranty expiry table and the alert cards. For a claim, tick the units and press **Prepare claim packet**, then **Download PDF** of the packet. There is no separate warranty spreadsheet export; for a spreadsheet use **Records → Grid → Export CSV** on Units.\n\n## Notifications, digests and outreach [article_id: team-and-notifications]\nDeepWell watches your records for expiring coverage and missing information, and tells the right people.\nQ: How do warranty alerts and the daily digest work?\nA: The **bell** in the header shows warranty and attention alerts with a count; click one to jump to it, or **Mark all read**. The daily digest email has a company-wide switch: in **Team → Settings → Notifications**, an admin turns **Send the company's daily warranty digest (every admin)** on or off. One email a day, only when something needs attention, sent to every company admin from alert@deepwelltechnology.com. To stop it for yourself only, use **Mute my daily digest** in the same place; other admins still get theirs.\nQ: How do I mute the daily digest just for me?\nA: Open **Team → Settings → Notifications** and turn on **Mute my daily digest**. It stops the digest email for you only; other admins still get it, and the company-wide switch **Send the company's daily warranty digest (every admin)** is not changed. Only admins receive the digest, so members have nothing to mute. Turn the switch off again to get it back.\nQ: What is outreach?\nA: Open **Dashboard → Open Outreach** (or **Open in Outreach** on an alert). Press **Generate drafts**, open a draft, then **Approve** (or **Approve all**); **Copy email** or **Open in mail** to send it yourself, or **Send approved (N)** when email sending is set up (admin). **Skip** drops one and **Sent log** lists what went out. In the collapsed Settings, choose **Review first** or **Automatic** (paid add-on; ask hello@deepwelltechnology.com). Only admins change settings.\nQ: What are follow-ups to team members?\nA: When a document is missing something only the team member who did the job knows, such as a serial, DeepWell can send a follow-up. An admin opens **Team → Follow-ups**, turns on **Send follow-up messages** (and **Also email** if wanted), and works the \"Currently due\" list with **Send now**, **Copy** or **Open in mail**.\nQ: Can members see billing or change team settings?\nA: Members can open Billing but can't change anything. Billing, invites, data export or deletion, support access, merging customers and sending outreach are admin only; a member sees those buttons disabled with \"Ask an admin\" beside them (Export CSV, customer merge, Billing actions, API keys), and Empty documents and Delete document are hidden from members. If a request still reaches the server it says \"This action requires the 'admin' role in your company.\" Members can ask Donovan, upload, browse and fix records. Ask an admin, or have one change your role in **Team**.\n\n## Security and privacy [article_id: security-and-privacy]\nDeepWell describes its real, current controls on the Security & Privacy page and in the Privacy Policy. This article does not round up: it lists what is not done yet, too.\nQ: Is my data secure?\nA: Yes. Your records are stored under your own company's account and kept separate from every other customer's, and the database enforces that separation on every query. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, and files sit in private storage that opens only through short-lived links. DeepWell staff have no standing access to your account: your admin can grant **support access** for a set time and revoke it at any time, and every access is recorded in your own activity log.\nQ: Can DeepWell see our data or files?\nA: DeepWell staff have no standing access to your account. Your records live under your company's own account, and the database enforces that isolation for every query. Inside the product, staff can look at your account only through **support access** that your admin grants for a set time and can revoke at any time, or in an emergency that is always logged where your admin can see it. Every access is recorded in your own activity log. The two founders also administer the hosting, database and file-storage accounts.\nQ: Is my data isolated from other customers?\nA: Yes. Every document, customer record and answer is stored under your company's account and is never pooled with another customer's data. The database enforces this at the row level on every query, not only in application code.\nQ: Is my data encrypted?\nA: Data is encrypted in transit with HTTPS/TLS, and files and database records are encrypted at rest by our storage providers (Cloudflare and Neon). Per-tenant encryption keys are not implemented: each customer's data is isolated by the database, not by separate keys.\nQ: Is DeepWell SOC 2 certified or compliant?\nA: No. DeepWell has **no SOC 2 or equivalent certification** yet, and it hasn't had an independent third-party audit. The controls described on the Security & Privacy page are real, but I can't claim a certification. For a security questionnaire, email security@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Does DeepWell use my documents to train AI?\nA: No. To read documents and answer questions, DeepWell sends content and query text to its AI providers (Anthropic, and Voyage AI for search). Under those providers' API terms, that content is not used to train their models, and it is not shared with any other customer. AI answers can still be wrong, so check the citation.\nQ: Who are your subprocessors?\nA: Cloudflare R2 (file storage), Neon (database), Clerk (sign-in), Anthropic (AI reading and answering), Voyage AI (search), Inngest (background jobs, identifiers only), Vercel (hosting and cookieless analytics), Stripe (payments), Resend (email) and Sentry (scrubbed error monitoring). All are US-based. See the Privacy Policy for the full table.\nQ: Are files private?\nA: Yes. Uploaded files are not public. Each time a document is opened, DeepWell issues a short-lived signed link for that one file, so a leaked link can't be reused for long and a file can't be found by guessing a URL.\nQ: Does DeepWell use cookies or advertising trackers?\nA: No tracking or advertising cookies, and no cookie banner. The only cookies are strictly necessary sign-in cookies from our authentication provider. Site analytics are cookieless.\nQ: What if I find a security problem?\nA: Please tell us before anyone else: **security@deepwelltechnology.com**. We acknowledge real reports and work with you on a fix. There is no formal published breach-notification deadline yet. Our commitment is to notify affected account admins without undue delay after confirming a breach.\nQ: Where can I read the privacy policy or terms?\nA: They are at deepwelltechnology.com/privacy and deepwelltechnology.com/terms, with a plain-language security summary at deepwelltechnology.com/security. I can't give legal advice. For a contract or DPA question, email privacy@deepwelltechnology.com or support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## Support access grants [article_id: support-access-grants]\nDeepWell support does not have standing access to your documents. You decide if and when.\nQ: How does support access work?\nA: An admin opens **Team → Support access** (a collapsed card), picks **Grant for** 24 hours, 72 hours or 7 days (the maximum), adds an optional reason (up to 500 characters) and presses **Grant support access**. It is off by default and nothing creates a grant automatically.\nQ: Can I see what support looked at?\nA: Yes. **Team → Support access → Access log (N)** lists every staff access: action, time, record count and, for emergency access, an \"emergency\" marker and the reason. It never shows the records themselves. Before any access it says \"No staff access recorded yet.\" Uploads, edits and exports are in the account activity log too.\nQ: What is emergency or break-glass access?\nA: For a genuine incident where you need help right now and no admin can be reached, staff can proceed without a grant only with an explicit, logged reason. It always shows up in your Access log. It's trust-based and not pre-approved, and that is one of the gaps we list openly.\n\n## Deleting data and closing your account [article_id: data-export-and-deletion]\nYou can delete a document, or the whole company's data, without waiting on us.\nQ: How do I delete a document?\nA: You can delete any document from your account at any time. Deletion removes it from both the file vault and the search index within our normal processing cycle.\nQ: How do I delete all my data or close my account?\nA: An admin opens **Team → Settings → Delete this company**, presses **Delete company data…**, types the company name and presses **Permanently delete**. It cancels the subscription first, and if that fails nothing is deleted. Export your data first if you want a copy. You can also ask privacy@deepwelltechnology.com, or I can send your request to the team.\nQ: What is kept after deletion?\nA: Deletion empties the company's documents, extracted facts and activity data. We keep a minimal account record (the company name or ID, plan and billing status), a deletion receipt and Stripe's own billing records, which we can't erase from Stripe. Database backups age out on the provider's retention window. Deletion doesn't remove people's sign-in accounts, which are removed separately.\nQ: What happens to my data if I cancel?\nA: You may request an export or deletion after canceling. We may suspend an account for non-payment or a terms violation, and after termination you can request an export for a reasonable period before it is deleted. Export from Team → Settings while you still have access.\n\n## Contacting the DeepWell team [article_id: contacting-humans]\nReal people answer. Pick the address that matches your question.\nQ: How do I contact DeepWell?\nA: All addresses end in @deepwelltechnology.com. **hello@** for sales and demos, **support@** for help using DeepWell, **billing@** for invoices and charges, **privacy@** for privacy and data requests, and **security@** to report a security concern.\nQ: Can I talk to a real person?\nA: Yes. I can send your question to the team from this chat. Choose **Send to a person**, add your email and we'll reply by email. Or write to support@deepwelltechnology.com directly.\nQ: How fast will support respond?\nA: Response targets depend on the plan: Solo, email with a next-business-day response. Team, email and chat, same business day. Crew, email, chat and phone, 2 hours for urgent issues. Fleet, a named contact, 1 hour for urgent issues, 24/7. I can't make promises beyond those listed targets. Phone support is listed for Crew and Fleet, so email support@ to get set up.\nQ: How do I talk to sales or get a demo?\nA: Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com. The best first step is to send a sample box, and on the first call you ask real questions about your own business. Fleet pricing beyond the base is quoted by email.\nQ: Can I ask a question before I sign up?\nA: Yes. On the DeepWell website, the **Talk to us** section at the bottom of the home page has a short form: add your name, company and work email, say roughly how many documents you have and where they are, and type your question. Sterling and Hilton read every one and reply by email within one business day. You can also just email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Who will I work with during setup?\nA: Sterling Chapman works with you from your first sample through go-live. Hilton Chapman leads customer relationships. Fleet customers get a named contact. Crew includes a scheduled onboarding call.\nQ: I need help with something urgent\nA: Email support@deepwelltechnology.com with what you see and when it started. Urgent-issue response targets are listed for Crew (2 hours) and Fleet (1 hour, 24/7). I can also send it to the team from here. You can also check status.deepwelltechnology.com to see whether DeepWell is up right now.\nQ: Is there a status page?\nA: Yes. The public status page is at status.deepwelltechnology.com. It shows whether the website, the app, the phone app and records and answers are up right now, with a history of past incidents. An uptime SLA is **coming soon** and is not in place today, including the 99.5% uptime SLA on Fleet. If something looks down, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## What is not available yet [article_id: known-limits-and-coming-soon]\nThese items are marked coming soon on the website, or are called out as not done in our security notes. I can't promise dates or that they will ship.\nQ: What features are coming soon?\nA: Nothing here has a date, and I can't promise one. Live today: ask donovan, phone app scanning, warranty tracking and export, bulk upload, records search, public status page, help chat. Marked **coming soon** on the site, being built next: email and folder upload, google drive sync, branch scoping, callback analytics, backups and per-company restore, uptime sla. Later, not available today: electrical, plumbing, property management, fleet and equipment rental.\nQ: Does DeepWell make backups?\nA: Daily off-site backups with a 30-day restore are marked coming soon on the Crew plan, and 6-hourly backups with per-company restore on Fleet. They aren't available as a feature today. Our database provider keeps its own point-in-time history, which ages out on its own retention window. You can export your data yourself any time.\nQ: What are the known security gaps?\nA: Openly: no SOC 2 or equivalent certification yet, no per-tenant encryption keys (isolation is enforced by the database), no formal published breach-notification deadline, and emergency support access is trust-based but always logged and visible to you. Bundling all original files into one zip export is not built yet either.\nQ: Is there a desktop or App Store app?\nA: DeepWell is a web app. On a computer, use deepwelltechnology.com/app. The phone app installs from your browser and isn't in an app store.\nQ: Can DeepWell check who is generating callbacks?\nA: Technician callback analytics are marked coming soon and are not available today.\n\n## Quick fixes for common problems [article_id: troubleshooting]\nMost problems have a short fix. If yours isn't here, I can pass it to the team.\nQ: I can't sign in\nA: Check that you're signing in with the email your invite went to, and use the password option on the sign-in page. If a phone home-screen app asks you to sign in again, sign in once inside the app, since it keeps its own sign-in. Still stuck: email support@deepwelltechnology.com. Never send a password.\nQ: My invite email didn't arrive\nA: Ask the person to check spam or junk. Confirm the address is right in **Team**, and re-send the invite if needed. Invites count toward your plan's login limit, and if you're at the limit the invite is blocked with a message that says so.\nQ: An upload failed\nA: Check the file type (PDF, JPG, PNG, GIF, WEBP, TXT, MD, CSV, TSV, JSON, DOCX or XLSX; a ZIP only in Inbox bulk import) and size (PDFs and photos under 24 MB, text, CSV, Word and Excel under 20 MB). Old .doc and .xls files, macro files and password-protected files aren't read: re-save them as .docx or .xlsx. \"Choose a plan to get started\", \"Subscription required\" or \"Monthly page limit reached\" mean uploads are paused for billing reasons (**See plans**). \"Daily AI budget reached\" resumes tomorrow. \"Couldn't reach DeepWell\" means check your connection and retry. \"Already on file\" means that exact file is already in. Otherwise email support@deepwelltechnology.com with the file name and time.\nQ: Donovan gave a wrong or missing answer\nA: Open the cited source and check it. The document may still be processing, or a field may be flagged or misread. Correct it in Records, then ask again. If it still looks wrong, tell us at support@deepwelltechnology.com with the question. Don't paste customer details you don't need to.\nQ: I can't see the Dashboard or Team screen\nA: Some screens and actions are for admins. Team is hidden from members, and if a member reaches it they see a read-only list of members. Billing, invites, exports and deletions need an admin. A member sees those buttons disabled with \"Ask an admin\" beside them (Export CSV, customer merge, Billing actions, API keys), and Empty documents and Delete document are hidden. Ask your company's admin. On a phone the app only has Ask, Scan and Docs, so use the desktop app for the rest.\nQ: I get \"API access is included on the Fleet plan\"\nA: API keys are a Fleet-only feature, so other plans can't create them. Upgrade to Fleet from Billing, or email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: The page looks broken or won't load\nA: Refresh the page and try a different browser or a private window. Then check your connection. If DeepWell still won't load, email support@deepwelltechnology.com with your browser, device and what you see. I can send that to the team from here.\n\n## Getting around the app [article_id: getting-around-the-app]\nThe desktop app has four main screens in the top bar (Ask, Dashboard, Inbox, Records) plus Billing, Team and sign out. The phone app has three tabs: Ask, Scan and Docs.\nQ: What are the main screens and where do I find things?\nA: Desktop top bar: **Ask** (questions to Donovan), **Dashboard** (warranty alerts and data health), **Inbox** (add files and things that need you), **Records** (customers, documents, grid, graph). At the right: the bell, **Billing**, **Team** and **Donovan** (admins only), Field/Office view, the company switcher and **Sign out**. On a narrow window only icons show. Phone: **Ask**, **Scan** and **Docs** tabs at the bottom.\nQ: What does the number on Inbox mean?\nA: It is how many documents need a person right now, the same count as **Inbox → Needs you** and the **Needs a person** chip. It drops as you answer questions and resolve the flagged items.\nQ: What is Field view and Office view, and how do I switch between light and dark?\nA: **Office view** is dark; **Field view** is light with larger type so it reads outdoors. Tap the sun or moon button in the top bar (desktop) or the header (phone) to switch. The choice is remembered on that device. Field view also gives the Ask screen field-style example questions.\nQ: Where is the DeepWell Help chat?\nA: Desktop: the round button at the bottom right of every screen, titled **DeepWell Help**. Phone: the same round button in the header. It answers questions about using DeepWell (not about your own records, which go to Ask). If it can't help, use **Send this to a person** and the team replies by email.\nQ: Is there a quick way to jump to a customer, serial or screen?\nA: On the desktop press **Ctrl+K** (or **Cmd+K** on a Mac) to open \"Jump to a customer, address, serial, document, or screen…\". Type a few letters, use the arrow keys and **Enter**. Results are grouped: Screens, Customers, Addresses, Units, Service visits, Technicians, Documents, Ask. **Esc** closes it. The old separate Search screen was folded into this and the search boxes in Records.\nQ: How do I share or bookmark a link to a unit or a screen?\nA: In the Dashboard's warranty table each unit has **Copy link**; anyone signed in to your company who opens it lands on that unit. Links with `?screen=billing` open Billing. For an answer, use **Share** on the Ask screen.\nQ: Why does my screen look different from the phone app?\nA: The phone app is for the field: **Ask**, **Scan** and **Docs**. Dashboard, the Inbox review queue, Team, Billing, exports and settings are desktop only. Sign out and switching companies are on the phone too, under the round profile button at the top right.\nQ: Can DeepWell schedule jobs, take payments, text customers or change my logo?\nA: DeepWell is a records system: it reads your paperwork, links it to customers and equipment, answers questions and watches warranties. It has no job scheduling or dispatch, payments, payroll, GPS tracking, customer texting, shipping labels, or branding or logo settings. The customer emails it drafts are warranty outreach (Dashboard → Open Outreach). If something you need is missing, tell support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## Fixing and verifying records [article_id: review-and-fix-records]\nWhen DeepWell can't be sure of something it leaves a short job in **Inbox → Needs you**. Anyone on the team can fix and verify records. Deleting a document and merging customers are admin only.\nQ: Where do I fix a document that needs info?\nA: Open **Inbox** and choose the **Needs you** tab (the badge is the count). Chips narrow the list: **Decisions** (quick questions), **Needs a person**, **Missing info**, **Needs linking**, **Conflicts**, **Duplicates**, **Ready to verify**, **Company records**, **Money to check** (only when there are money issues) and **All**. Pick one, open a document and work through it. The Dashboard's Data health tiles open the matching chip.\nQ: How do I answer DeepWell's questions in Decisions?\nA: **Inbox → Needs you → Decisions** shows one card per question. Click the right option (or press 1 to 9). If none fits choose **Type it instead**, type the value and press **Confirm**. **Why are we asking?** shows the evidence. The clock button asks again later (S), and the x means it doesn't apply. The \"On file for this document\" chips have a check (**Looks right**) and a pencil (**Fix**). When it's empty: \"Nothing needs a decision right now.\"\nQ: How do I correct a wrong serial number or other field?\nA: Open the document from **Inbox → Needs you** (or **Records → Documents**). Under **Extracted fields**, fix the value; a required field that's missing has a box and an **Add** button. On a Decisions card use the pencil (**Fix**) beside the field. Your correction is used for later answers. On the phone open the document from **Docs** and answer under **Needs your input**.\nQ: How do I mark a document as checked or verified?\nA: Click **Looks right** (the check) on a field you've confirmed. When nothing is left to resolve, the button at the bottom of the document reads **Mark checked** (or **Advance to <stage>**). If it's greyed out, a line says what's blocking: choose a document type, add the missing field, link it to a record or settle a disputed value. Checked documents count toward answers.\nQ: How do I set or change a document's type?\nA: Open the document and use the **Document type** buttons in its review panel. The required fields update to match the type. A document with no type shows as \"Unclassified\".\nQ: How do I link a document to a customer or a unit?\nA: Open the document. In **Customer** press **Link to <name>** if DeepWell suggests one, or **Change customer…**, search by name and press **Use this**, or type a name under \"Or create a new customer…\". Under **Linked to** you can also pick a record in \"Record to link\" and press **Link**. If two customers share a name it asks you to confirm which one. From a customer's profile you can also **Assign a document to this customer**.\nQ: Two documents disagree. What do I do?\nA: Open the **Conflicts** chip. The panel says \"Two documents disagree on <field>\" and shows each value with its source. Click the one that is right. Open each source first if you're not sure.\nQ: What do I do with a duplicate document?\nA: Open **Inbox → Needs you → Duplicates**, open the copy and press **Merge into original**. The original stays and the copy is dropped, so nothing is double counted. An upload with identical contents is caught automatically (\"Already on file\").\nQ: How do I merge duplicate customers?\nA: Admins can merge; a member sees the merge buttons disabled with \"Ask an admin\" beside them, and the whole-company scan is hidden. In **Records → Customers**, a banner lists likely pairs: **Merge into <name>** (tick which one to keep), **Not the same**, or **Merge all**. Admins also get a whole-company **Duplicate customers** scan there, with Undo after a merge. The same suggestions appear in Inbox → Needs you. A different name at the same address is never merged automatically.\nQ: What does Verify with AI do?\nA: On a document that isn't checked yet, **Verify with AI** has DeepWell re-check it. You'll see \"Verified by AI.\" or \"Not confident enough yet — this still needs a person.\" AI-verified documents show an **AI verified** badge.\nQ: How do I open the original file?\nA: Press **Open original** in the document's review panel, or click a citation or a row in Records and use **Download <file name>** in the preview. On the phone use **Open original** in the document sheet.\nQ: How do I delete a document?\nA: An admin opens the document (**Inbox → Needs you**, then the document) and presses **Delete document**, then **Confirm delete**. It can't be undone. Members don't see the **Delete document** button at all; ask an admin.\nQ: How do I correct an invoice amount or total?\nA: Open the invoice. **Money on this document** lists Number, Date, Due, Subtotal, Tax, Total, Paid, Balance due and Status. Press **Correct <field>** beside a value, type the right one and save. The **Money to check** chip lists invoices where the numbers didn't add up.\nQ: What are company records and Hide company records?\nA: **Company records** are documents about your own company (typed Internal) rather than a customer's job. They have their own chip in Needs you, with an optional technician filter. Tick **Hide company records** to keep them out of the other chips.\nQ: What does Find reminders do?\nA: On the **Needs linking** chip, **Find reminders** scans the unlinked documents for notes like \"check the filter next visit\" and attaches them to the right customer. A customer's profile lists them under **Open reminders**.\nQ: How do I answer a question about a scan on my phone?\nA: Open the document from **Docs** (or tap \"needs 1 answer\" on a scan result). Under **Needs your input** tap the right option or type the value. You'll see \"All set — nothing else needs an answer on this document.\" Bigger clean-up (linking, merging, deleting) is on the desktop.\n\n## The Billing screen, trial and usage [article_id: billing-screen]\nBilling is in the header (icon and \"Billing\"). Every member can open it and read the plan and usage; only admins can change anything. A member sees the Billing buttons disabled, with \"Ask an admin\" beside them and a note that only a company admin can start a plan, change it or manage billing.\nQ: How do I start my free trial?\nA: An admin opens **Billing** and presses **Start 30-day free trial**. It is the Solo plan, a card is required, and nothing is charged until the 30 days end. It is offered only to a company that has never subscribed. You can cancel any time before it ends from **Manage billing**.\nQ: It says \"Pick a plan to open your account\". Why?\nA: A company with no plan (never subscribed, or canceled) can only open **Billing** and **Team** until an admin picks a plan. On the phone it says \"Choose a plan to continue\" and the owner picks one on the desktop app. Nothing is deleted; your records are there when a plan is active again.\nQ: What is Manage billing?\nA: **Billing → Manage billing** (in the Current plan card, shown once a plan exists) opens Stripe's billing portal. There an admin updates the card, views invoices and receipts, and cancels. A member sees it disabled with \"Ask an admin\".\nQ: Where can I see my usage against my plan?\nA: Open **Billing** and look at the **Current plan** card: **Logins**, **Documents stored** and **Pages this month**, each as used / cap. Donovan questions are unlimited, and the owner isn't counted toward logins.\nQ: What do Free trial, Active, Payment failed and Canceled mean?\nA: The pill on Billing shows **Free trial**, **Active**, **Payment failed**, **Canceled** or **No plan yet**. A banner says \"Your free trial ends in N days\" or \"Your last payment failed. Update billing to keep uploading.\" (**Go to Billing**). If a payment has been failing for more than 7 days uploads stop with \"Subscription required\" until the card is fixed.\nQ: I paid or canceled checkout and Billing shows a message. What does it mean?\nA: After Stripe you land back on Billing. \"Billing updated — thanks!\" means it worked. \"Checkout canceled — nothing was charged.\" means you backed out. \"Confirming your subscription…\" can show for up to a minute while Stripe reports in; refresh once after a minute. If it still shows the old plan, email billing@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: How do I buy Records Rescue?\nA: An admin opens **Billing → Records Rescue**, enters the number of **Pages** (a minimum applies) and presses **Buy Records Rescue**. It is a one-time purchase for paper scanning and is separate from your subscription.\nQ: How do I create an API key?\nA: On the **Fleet** plan an admin opens **Billing → API access**, types a **Key name** and presses **Create key**. The key (starts dw_live_) is shown once, so copy it right away: \"Copy your new key now — it will not be shown again\". Keys can read, ingest and ask. **Revoke** on a row turns one off. A member on a Fleet company sees \"API keys are managed by a company admin. Ask an admin.\" instead of the key form.\nQ: Where is API access? I don't see it.\nA: API keys are Fleet only. On other plans **Billing** shows \"API access is included on the Fleet plan. Upgrade to connect your own systems to DeepWell with API keys.\" with a **See Fleet** button.\n\n## Using the phone app [article_id: phone-app-how-to]\nThe phone app (deepwelltechnology.com/m) has three tabs: **Ask**, **Scan** and **Docs**. Your last tab is remembered.\nQ: What do I see after I scan a document on my phone?\nA: Each uploaded page shows \"Uploaded and read\" (or \"Uploaded — still being read\", or \"Already in DeepWell — nothing new to add\"), then \"Filled X of Y fields\", then \"— all set\" or \"— needs 1 answer\". Tap the row to answer in the document sheet.\nQ: I have no signal. Can I still scan?\nA: Yes. With no signal the scan is saved on the phone (\"No signal — saved on your phone, will upload automatically\") and listed under **Waiting to upload (N)** on the Scan tab. It retries by itself when the phone is back online or you reopen the app. If the session expired a **Sign in again** button appears. You can remove a row from the queue; files that are too large or rejected stay listed until you remove them.\nQ: My phone scan says I need to pick a plan.\nA: When a plan or page-limit block stops a phone upload, the row shows the message and a **See plans** button. The owner or an admin fixes it in **Billing** on the desktop app. The scan is not lost.\nQ: Do the phone tabs stay when I switch?\nA: Yes. The tab you were on is remembered and an Ask thread stays while you switch to Scan or Docs. The header shows the company name, **Help**, the Field/Office view button and the round profile button (your initial), which opens the **Account** sheet.\nQ: Why does my phone say \"Join your company first\" or \"Choose a plan to continue\"?\nA: \"Join your company first\" means the account isn't in a company yet: accept your invite email, or ask an admin to invite you. \"Choose a plan to continue\" means the company has no active plan; the owner picks one in **Billing** on the desktop app (**See plans**).\nQ: How do I find a document on my phone?\nA: Open the **Docs** tab. Search \"Customer, address, serial…\", or tap **Filters** (Type, Status, Warranty, Site / address, then **Apply** or **Clear**), **Sort**, or **Group by customer**. Tap a row for the document sheet (customer, missing fields, **Open original**); tap the customer for their sheet with Equipment, Recent documents and **Call**.\nQ: How do I ask Donovan on my phone?\nA: Open the **Ask** tab, type in \"Ask Donovan…\" or tap a starter, and send. Answers show sources you can tap. It needs a connection; on a weak signal a slow answer says \"That took too long — probably a weak signal. Try again.\" Questions typed into the Help chat can be passed to Ask.\nQ: Where do I sign out or switch companies on the phone?\nA: Tap the round profile button (your initial) at the top right of the phone app. The **Account** sheet shows your name and email, the **Current company**, and **Sign out**. If you belong to more than one company it also lists them under **Switch company**; tapping one reloads the app on that company. If scans are still waiting to upload, signing out warns you first: \"N scans have not been sent yet. Signing out deletes them from this phone.\" Choose **Stay signed in** to keep them, or **Sign out and delete**. Scans waiting to upload stay with the company they were taken in, so switching companies never sends them to the wrong one; they upload when that company is active again.\n\n## Finding customers, documents and equipment [article_id: finding-records]\nRecords opens on **Documents** the first time you use it, then remembers the last tab you used. Search, filters and views all live inside its tabs.\nQ: Where are my documents and customers?\nA: Open **Records**. The tabs are **Documents** (where a new user lands first), **Customers**, **Grid** and **Graph**. Records reopens on the tab you used last. Your uploaded files are under **Documents**. The old separate Search screen is gone: use the search boxes in Customers and Documents, or press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on a Mac).\nQ: How do I search my documents?\nA: **Records → Documents**. The box reads \"Search filename, customer, address, technician, brand, contents…\". Results show as a table (Name, Type, Customer, Address, Date, Tech, Status, Amount) or as cards; click a row to preview it. To ask about what's inside, use the Ask screen instead.\nQ: How do I filter documents by type, status or warranty?\nA: In **Records → Documents** press **Filters**. You can filter by Type, Status (Verified, Needs review, Missing info), Warranty (Expired, Expiring 90 days, Active, No warranty on file), Customer, Site, Technician, Brand, Money (Has money, Open balance), My uploads, Service date range and Upload date range. Active filters show as chips; **Clear all** resets them.\nQ: How do I sort or group documents?\nA: In **Records → Documents**: **Sort** (Newest upload, Newest service date, Customer A–Z, Type, Amount), **Group** (No grouping, Customer, Type, Month, Site) and the table/card buttons. The **Audience** control switches between Customer, Internal and All; Internal documents are team-only and badged \"Team only\".\nQ: How do I save a filtered view?\nA: In **Records → Documents** set your filters and press **Save current view**, name it and **Save**. Built-in views are **Needs review**, **Warranties expiring 90 days**, **This month's invoices** and **My uploads**. Delete one with the x. Views are saved in this browser only, but the URL holds the filters so you can share the link.\nQ: How do I search or filter customers?\nA: **Records → Customers**. Search \"Search by name, address, phone, or email…\". Filters: Alerts (Expiring soon, Expired, Needs attention, No alerts), Equipment (Has units, No units on file), City and Last activity (30, 90 or 365 days). Sort by Recent activity, Name A–Z, Address A–Z, Most documents, Most equipment or Alerts first. **Clear all** resets.\nQ: How do I add a customer?\nA: In **Records → Customers** press **New customer** and fill in Name, Address, Phone and Email. You usually don't need to: customers appear automatically as documents are read and matched.\nQ: What's on a customer's profile?\nA: Click a customer row. Click a value (Name, Address, Phone, Email) to edit and save it; Call and Email links sit beside them. Tiles show Documents, Equipment, Next warranty expiry and Open alerts, and tabs cover Documents, Equipment, Timeline, Graph and Notes (type, then **Save notes**). **Assign a document to this customer** links one from there.\nQ: What is the Grid?\nA: **Records → Grid** is a spreadsheet of Documents or Units. Use \"Filter by model or serial…\", the **Columns** picker (remembered), **Load more rows** or **Load all (up to 5,000)**, and **Export CSV (N rows)** to download what you see.\nQ: What is the Graph?\nA: **Records → Graph** (and the **Graph** toggle on a customer or record) draws customers, properties, equipment and documents and how they connect. Click a node to open it. It's for exploring; for a specific answer use the Ask screen.\nQ: Where is a unit's page?\nA: Click any serial (in an answer, the Dashboard, a customer's Equipment tab or the Ctrl+K search) to open the unit page: its fields with their sources, related service visits and \"Documents linked to this record\". The page also has an **Install date** box (see the next answer).\nQ: How do I add or change a unit's install date?\nA: Open the unit's page (click its serial, or press **Add install date** / **Change install date** in the Dashboard's warranty lists, which opens the page with the date box ready). In the **Install date** box press **Add install date** (or **Change install date**), pick the date and press **Save**. Anyone signed in to your company who can correct records can do this, members included. The date must be after 1950 and no more than about three months ahead. The page then shows \"entered by\" your name and the date it was typed; a date that came from a scanned document shows the document as its source. If DeepWell has a verified rule for that brand, the warranty is worked out from the new date right away; a printed expiry already on a document is kept, and a brand with no verified rule keeps the date but gets no computed expiry.\n\n## Asking Donovan step by step [article_id: asking-donovan-how-to]\nDonovan answers questions about your own records on the **Ask** screen (desktop) or **Ask** tab (phone).\nQ: How do I ask a question?\nA: Open **Ask**, type in the box (\"Ask Donovan anything — an address, a serial, a name, a question…\") and press **Enter**. **Shift+Enter** starts a new line and **Esc** clears the box. Suggestions appear as you type, and the small pill under the box says what Donovan will search. Plain wording works; you don't need a special format.\nQ: Where do I get example questions or my recent ones?\nA: Before your first question the Ask screen shows **Try asking** chips built from your own records (or \"For example\" samples) and a **Recent** list of past questions you can click to ask again. Field view uses field-style examples.\nQ: How do I see where an answer came from?\nA: Every answer carries citations: numbered [1] markers and source chips. Click one to open the document. When nothing is found it shows \"Closest documents\", and for counts a records panel lists the rows behind the number.\nQ: What does Include unverified do?\nA: By default Donovan searches checked (verified) records. Turn on **Include unverified** to also search documents that were read but not checked yet. The caption under the answer says \"Searched verified records only\" or \"Searched linked and verified records\". Treat unverified facts with care.\nQ: Can I ask a follow-up question?\nA: Yes. Type the next question and Donovan builds on the last four (\"Following up on N earlier questions\"). Click a follow-up chip under an answer for suggestions. **New question** starts fresh.\nQ: Donovan says \"Nothing in your records answers that.\" What now?\nA: That means the records don't contain it, or it isn't checked yet. Look at the **Did you mean** chips and \"Closest documents\", try **Include unverified**, or check that the paperwork was uploaded and finished (Inbox). A **Not on file** badge marks the miss.\nQ: How do I tell Donovan an answer was wrong?\nA: Under an answer use **Was this right?**: thumbs up or thumbs down. A thumbs-down opens \"What was wrong? (optional)\"; it is logged and Donovan re-checks. Then open the cited source and correct the record if a field was misread.\nQ: How do I share or copy an answer?\nA: Use **Share** on an answer to copy or share it, and the copy button next to a value to copy just that value.\nQ: How do I ask about a serial number from a photo?\nA: On the desktop Ask screen tap the camera icon in the box (\"Serial from photo\"), **Take a photo of the label**, then confirm or edit the serial it read. Donovan then asks about that serial. On the phone you can also photograph a nameplate on the **Scan** tab to file it.\nQ: Donovan shows an error. What does it mean?\nA: \"Donovan couldn't get an answer\" plus a reason: try again. \"Your session has expired. Reload the page and sign in again.\" \"Daily AI budget reached — resumes tomorrow.\" \"Donovan is seeing unusually high usage on your account\" means email support@deepwelltechnology.com. A billing message shows **See plans**. On the phone, \"That took too long — probably a weak signal. Try again.\"\n\n## Dashboard, warranty alerts and claim packets [article_id: dashboard-and-alerts]\nThe **Dashboard** is where warranty expirations and data health live.\nQ: What is on the Dashboard?\nA: Collapsible sections: **Data health** (Documents, AI verified, Needs linking, Missing info, Conflicts; duplicates are held out of every count), **Financials** (admin), **Alerts**, **Overview** (Documents, Units on record), **Warranty expiry · next to expire first**, **Equipment at risk** and **Customer outreach**. Data health tiles open the matching chip in Inbox → Needs you.\nQ: What do the alert cards mean and what can I do with them?\nA: Cards: **Expired**, **This quarter (30+90d)**, **Expiring in 30 days**, **Expiring in 90 days**, **Expiring in 12 months**, **Registration closing** and **Upsell candidates**. Open one to see its units; each has **View customer**, **Ask about this unit**, **Open in Outreach**, **Dismiss** (then **Undo**) and a checkbox to add it to a claim packet.\nQ: How do I see which warranties are expiring?\nA: On the **Dashboard**, the **Warranty expiry · next to expire first** table has **All** and **This quarter**, with Unit, Location, Expires and Status. Each row has **Copy link**, **Ask** and **Ask: next 12 months**. Below are \"Covered\" and \"No warranty on file — needs install date\" lists; **Add install date** (or **Change install date** when one is on file) opens that unit's page with the date box ready. Type or pick the date and press **Save**; if DeepWell has a verified rule for the brand, the warranty is worked out from it right away.\nQ: How do I prepare a warranty claim packet?\nA: Tick units in the Dashboard alerts or table and press **Prepare claim packet (N)**. In **Warranty claim packet** you can add a unit, **Select all** or **Clear**, remove one with the x, check the **Packet preview** and press **Download PDF**. The PDF stays disabled until every unit has verified documents; the reason shows (\"Warranty expired\", \"Missing …\" or \"No verified documents\"). Check the documents in Inbox → Needs you first.\nQ: What is the Financials card?\nA: Admins see **Financials** on the Dashboard: totals Donovan counted from your invoices, and a note of what it couldn't count. An admin can start the backfill there to pick up older invoices. Wrong figures are corrected on the invoice under \"Money on this document\".\nQ: What is the Donovan button in the header?\nA: Admins only. **Donovan** opens Answer quality: **misses** (questions Donovan couldn't answer, to replay or copy for review), **learning** (proposals you can keep as tests), the **scorecard** (**Run scorecard**) and **Search by meaning → Prepare older documents**. Members don't see it.\n\n## Team screen, exports and deleting data [article_id: team-and-data-how-to]\nTeam is admin only in the header; its cards are Phone app for your team, Follow-ups, Settings and Support access, plus the invite form and, below it, our sign-in provider's panel with **Members** and **Invitations** tabs (change a role, remove someone, cancel an invitation).\nQ: Where is the QR code to put the app on my team's phones?\nA: An admin opens **Team → Phone app for your team**: a QR code they can scan, **Copy install link** to text or email, and **See install steps** for iPhone and Android.\nQ: How do I revoke support access?\nA: An admin opens **Team → Support access**. While a grant is active it says \"Access active until <date>\"; press **Revoke now**.\nQ: How do I empty all of my documents but keep the company?\nA: An admin opens **Records → Documents**, finds \"Empty this company's documents\", types **DELETE** and presses **Empty documents**. It is permanent, so export first (**Team → Settings → Your data**). To remove just one, use **Delete document** on it. Members don't see **Empty documents** or **Delete document**; ask an admin.";
// Public-website articles only (audience: public). The model prefix for signed-out visitors is built from THIS, never MODEL_KB.
export const MODEL_KB_PUBLIC = "## What DeepWell is [article_id: what-is-deepwell]\nDeepWell is a hosted records system for any business that stores documents or paperwork. It reads your invoices, work orders, contracts, forms and photos of documents, links them to the right customer and address, and lets the team ask questions in plain language. Every answer shows its source. Equipment paperwork such as warranties, serial numbers and service tickets is where it understands the most today.\nQ: What is DeepWell?\nA: DeepWell finds the answer in your own records. Your invoices, work orders, contracts, forms and photos of documents go in, DeepWell reads them and links each fact to the right customer and address (and, for equipment paperwork, the right unit), and your team asks questions the way they would ask a coworker. Every answer shows the source document. We set it up for you, so day one is already useful.\nQ: Who is DeepWell for?\nA: DeepWell is for any small or mid-sized business that stores documents or paperwork, from an owner-operator to a multi-team company. Equipment paperwork such as warranties, serial numbers and service tickets is where it is deepest today. Office staff use it to answer callers, people in the field use it on a phone, and owners use it to see expiring warranties and agreements.\nQ: Do you support electrical, plumbing or property management?, electrical contractors, just hvac, only hvac\nA: You can upload electrical, plumbing or property-management paperwork today, because DeepWell reads any business documents. What is not live yet are the industry-specific features, such as backflow-test tracking or lease handling. Those pages are on the site and marked coming soon, with no dates. You can join the waitlist from those pages or email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Will DeepWell work for my business?\nA: If your business keeps documents or paperwork, yes. DeepWell reads invoices, contracts, permits, forms, correspondence and photos of documents, files them by customer and address, and answers questions with the original page attached. Equipment paperwork (warranties, serials, service tickets) is where it understands the most today. It does not have industry-specific features for other fields yet, and I can't promise dates for them. Not sure? Send one sample box free and see the result before you commit.\nQ: How does DeepWell work?\nA: Three steps. **Ingest:** paper, PDFs, Word and Excel files, CSVs and photos go in as they are. **Link:** each document is read for serials, addresses, dates, names and amounts, and connected to the matching customer and equipment. **Ask:** you type a question and get the answer with the source page attached. Uncertain reads are flagged for a quick human check.\nQ: What kinds of records can DeepWell read?\nA: Invoices, work orders, contracts and agreements, permits, forms, purchase orders, inspection reports, correspondence and photos of documents, plus warranty cards, startup sheets, service tickets and nameplate photos. DeepWell reads handwritten and low-quality scans too. Nothing has to be renamed or filed first.\nQ: Who are the founders?\nA: DeepWell was founded by two brothers. **Hilton Chapman** is a retired Air Force veteran who leads customer relationships and marketing and sets the vision. **Sterling Chapman** has prior Army service and is the engineer behind the platform. He works with you from your first sample through go-live.\nQ: Where is DeepWell based?\nA: DeepWell Technology LLC is based in Alamogordo, New Mexico, USA.\nQ: Is there a free demo or sample?\nA: Yes. Send one sample box or folder of old invoices, tickets or warranties and we will digitize it free so you can see the result before you commit to the rest. Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com to start. Solo also has a 30-day free trial.\nQ: What is white-glove setup?\nA: Every plan includes setup by our team. We inventory your records, run the first bulk ingest, check the links against the questions your office actually asks, and train your crew in an afternoon.\n\n## Plans and pricing [article_id: plans-and-pricing]\nFour plans: Solo, Team, Crew and Fleet. All prices are in US dollars. Donovan, our question-answering assistant, is unlimited on every plan.\nQ: How much does DeepWell cost?\nA: Solo is $99/month, Team $199/month, Crew $399/month and Fleet $899+/month. Every plan includes unlimited Donovan, white-glove setup and data export. Plans differ by logins, storage, monthly scan volume and support. Full details are on the Pricing section of deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What does the Solo plan include?\nA: **Solo, $99/month**, for the owner-operator: up to 2 logins, 25,000 documents stored, 750 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, email support with a next-business-day response, and a 30-day free trial (card required).\nQ: What does the Team plan include?\nA: **Team, $199/month** (formerly Shop), for a small company: up to 5 logins, 100,000 documents stored, 2,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, and email plus chat support with a same-business-day response.\nQ: What does the Crew plan include?\nA: **Crew, $399/month**, for a growing crew: up to 10 logins, 500,000 documents stored, 5,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, email, chat and phone support with a 2-hour response for urgent issues, and a scheduled onboarding call.\nQ: What does the Fleet plan include?\nA: **Fleet, $899+/month**, for multi-crew teams: 11+ logins, unlimited documents stored, 10,000 new pages a month, unlimited Donovan, API access, a named contact (Sterling) from first sample to go-live, and a 1-hour response for urgent issues, 24/7. For Fleet pricing beyond the base, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What is included in every plan?\nA: Every plan includes unlimited Donovan with sources, white-glove setup by our team, and the ability to export your data anytime. A public status page is live at status.deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is there annual pricing or a discount?\nA: Yes. Pay annually and you get one month free, so a year costs 11 times the monthly price: Solo $1,089, Team $2,189, Crew $4,389 and Fleet $9,889. I can't offer other discounts or custom terms. For those, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is DeepWell priced per team member?\nA: No. Pricing is by plan tier, not per team member. Pick the plan that fits your team size, scan volume and support needs.\nQ: Which plan should I choose?\nA: Match the plan to your team. **Solo** fits an owner-operator with up to 2 logins. **Team** fits up to 5 logins. **Crew** fits up to 10. **Fleet** is for 11 or more logins or if you need API access. The owner account is not counted. Scan allowance grows with each plan: 750, 2,000, 5,000 and 10,000 pages a month.\nQ: Is Donovan really unlimited?\nA: Yes. Donovan is unlimited on every plan. There is a fair-use safety limit that ordinary use never reaches. It exists only to stop runaway automation.\nQ: Are there setup fees or contracts?\nA: Setup by our team is included with every plan, and I don't see a separate setup fee listed. Monthly plans can be canceled at any time. Annual prepay locks in the annual price. Records Rescue scanning is a separate paid service.\n\n## Free trial and billing states [article_id: trial-and-billing-dates]\nThe free trial is on Solo only. Billing has four states: trialing, active, past due and canceled.\nQ: Is there a free trial?\nA: Yes. Solo has a **30-day free trial**. A card is required, you won't be charged until the trial ends, and you can cancel anytime. Team, Crew and Fleet do not have a trial. If you want to see DeepWell on your own records first, ask about the free sample box.\nQ: Do I need a credit card for the trial?\nA: Yes, a card is required at checkout for the Solo trial. You won't be charged until the 30 days are over, and you can cancel before then.\nQ: Can I get a second free trial?\nA: The free trial is one per account. Canceling and signing up again does not start a new one. For an extension request, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What happens if my payment fails?\nA: You keep full access for a **7-day grace period** after the due date. After that, uploads pause, but you can still read and ask Donovan about your existing records. Update your card from **Billing → Manage billing** (admins only) to restore full access.\nQ: What happens when I cancel?\nA: Cancellation on a monthly plan takes effect at the end of the current billing period. Once a subscription has ended, you'll be asked to choose a plan to keep uploading and asking questions. You can export your data first; see the export article.\nQ: Where can I see my renewal or trial end date?\nA: Open **Billing** in the app. It shows your plan, status, trial end or renewal date and this month's usage. Admins can also open **Manage billing** for invoices and payment methods. If you ask me while signed in, I can look up your plan and dates.\nQ: What does \"Choose a plan to get started\" mean?\nA: Your account has no active plan, either because you haven't subscribed yet or the subscription has ended. Open **Billing** and pick a plan. Until then only Billing and Team are available.\n\n## Add-ons and Records Rescue [article_id: add-ons]\nThree things are sold on top of a plan: Records Rescue scanning, the automatic outreach add-on, and API access, which comes with Fleet.\nQ: What is Records Rescue?\nA: Records Rescue is our scanning service for old paper. Full service is **$0.12 per page with a $500 minimum**. It is billed separately from your plan and can be bought under Billing. It is non-refundable once scanning has begun. You can start with a free sample box first.\nQ: Can I try Records Rescue before paying?\nA: Yes. Send one sample folder or box of old invoices, tickets or warranties and we digitize it free so you can see the result before committing to the rest. Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com to arrange it.\nQ: What is the automatic outreach add-on?\nA: DeepWell can draft warranty-upsell emails to your customers when a unit's warranty is about to end. In review mode a person approves and sends each one, and that needs no add-on. The fully automatic, unattended sending is a paid add-on. For its price, email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Is API access an add-on?\nA: API access is included on the **Fleet** plan only. Fleet admins create and revoke API keys in the app. Other plans can't create keys. Ready-made integrations with other software are not listed as available today.\nQ: Does DeepWell integrate with QuickBooks or other software?\nA: No built-in integrations are listed as available today. Google Drive sync and email or folder intake are marked coming soon, with no date. You can export CSV for dispatch and accounting, and Fleet has API access.\n\n## Changing or canceling a plan, invoices, refunds [article_id: change-cancel-plan-invoices]\nQ: Can I cancel my plan at any time?\nA: You can cancel at any time. A monthly plan's cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period, and there are no prorated refunds for partial months. The 30-day Solo trial can also be canceled any time, and you aren't charged until it ends. If you'd like a person to handle it, I can send your request to the team.\nQ: What is your refund policy?\nA: Monthly plans are not refunded for partial months. Annual plans are refundable in full if you cancel within 30 days of the first annual payment, and non-refundable after that. Records Rescue is non-refundable once scanning has begun. If you believe you were billed in error, contact us within 30 days of the charge at support@deepwelltechnology.com. I can't issue refunds myself.\nQ: Does DeepWell store my credit card?\nA: No. Stripe, our payment processor, handles and stores your card details and processes payments directly. DeepWell stores your subscription and billing status and a Stripe customer ID, never your card number. Please don't type a card number into this chat.\nQ: Do you offer refunds for the free trial?\nA: You aren't charged during the 30-day Solo trial (a card is required to start), and you can cancel any time before it ends. If you were charged and believe it was a mistake, contact us within 30 days of the charge at support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## Uploading and scanning on the web app [article_id: uploading-and-scanning-web]\nQ: Which file types can I upload, and is there a size limit?\nA: DeepWell reads PDFs, photos (JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP), Word (.docx) and Excel (.xlsx) files, CSV and plain text. Old Word and Excel files (.doc, .xls), files with macros and password-protected files are not read: re-save them as .docx or .xlsx (or PDF). iPhone photos are converted to JPEG automatically in Safari; in another browser, set the iPhone camera to Most Compatible. Nothing has to be renamed or filed first, and it reads handwriting, carbon copies and low-quality scans. For an unusual format or very large files, I can pass the question to the team.\n\n## The phone app and how to install it [article_id: mobile-app-and-install]\nDeepWell Mobile installs from your browser. There is nothing to download from an app store and nothing to update.\nQ: Is there a DeepWell phone app?\nA: Yes. DeepWell Mobile works on iPhone, iPad and Android. It has three tabs: **Ask** for Donovan, **Scan** for photographing paperwork and **Docs** for finding documents. The full desktop app has everything else: Inbox, Records, Dashboard, Team and Billing.\nQ: How do I install the app on iPhone?\nA: Open **deepwelltechnology.com/m** in **Safari**. Tap **Share**, scroll down, tap **Add to Home Screen**, then **Add**. Open DeepWell from your home screen and sign in there. The home-screen app keeps its own sign-in.\nQ: How do I install the app on Android?\nA: Open **deepwelltechnology.com/m** in **Chrome**. Tap **Install** when DeepWell offers it, or open the menu and choose **Install app** or **Add to Home screen**. Then open DeepWell from your home screen and sign in.\nQ: Why isn't it in the App Store or Google Play?\nA: It installs straight from the browser, so everyone always has the latest version. It gets its own icon and opens full screen like any other app. There's no store listing, so search the store won't find it. Use the install steps above.\nQ: Does the phone app cost extra?\nA: No. The phone app is included with every plan. Your team members sign in with their own DeepWell accounts, which the company owner invites from Team.\nQ: Does it work with bad signal?\nA: It is built for weak signal: it opens quickly, photos are shrunk on the phone before uploading, and slow answers show a retry. The app itself opens from the phone with weak or no signal. Asking Donovan needs a connection. A scan taken with no signal is saved on the phone and uploads by itself when the signal returns (see Waiting to upload on the Scan tab).\nQ: The install button doesn't show up. What do I do?\nA: Open the page in **Safari** on iPhone or **Chrome** on Android. In-app browsers such as those inside social, email or messaging apps can't install DeepWell. Use the menu there and choose **Open in Safari** or **Open in Chrome**, then try again.\nQ: How do I scan paperwork with my phone?\nA: Open the **Scan** tab and tap **Take photo** (rear camera), then **Add another page** if needed, or **Choose photos or PDFs**. With several photos, choose **One document, N pages** or **N separate documents**, then tap **Upload N pages**. DeepWell reads and files it, then shows \"Uploaded and read\". Then **Scan another** or **View docs**.\n\n## Monthly page allowance and storage limits [article_id: page-allowance-and-limits]\nEach plan has a monthly allowance of new pages, a documents-stored limit and a login limit. Donovan questions are not limited.\nQ: How many pages can I scan per month?\nA: Solo: 750 new pages a month. Team: 2,000. Crew: 5,000. Fleet: 10,000. A page is one page of a document: for a PDF, one printed page; a photo is one page. A Word (.docx) file counts about one page for every 3,000 characters of text (about one printed page), at least one. An Excel (.xlsx) or CSV file counts one page for each block of roughly 6,000 characters of a sheet (the header row is repeated in every block), and every sheet that has anything in it counts at least one; an empty sheet counts none. Plain text, Markdown and JSON count one page for every 6,000 characters. Signed in, ask me and I'll check your usage.\nQ: How are pages counted for Word, Excel and CSV files?\nA: A Word (.docx) file counts about one page per 3,000 characters of text, at least one. An Excel (.xlsx) or CSV file counts one page per block of roughly 6,000 characters of a sheet (header row repeated in each block); an empty sheet counts none. The real count is set when the file is read. Before that DeepWell uses a size estimate, which errs high for files full of pictures (not read or counted) and can be much lower for very repetitive files. The final count is checked at reading: a file that would use more pages than you have left this month is not added and nothing is counted. Only the final count is added to your monthly pages.\nQ: How many documents can I store?\nA: Solo stores up to 25,000 documents, Team 100,000, Crew 500,000, and Fleet is unlimited.\nQ: What happens when I reach my page limit?\nA: New uploads pause with a message that the monthly page limit is reached. Existing records and Donovan keep working. Upgrade your plan for a larger allowance, or email support@deepwelltechnology.com. If you have a large backlog, Records Rescue can scan it separately.\nQ: Do questions to Donovan count against my allowance?\nA: No. Donovan is unlimited on every plan. Only new pages you scan or upload count toward the monthly page allowance.\nQ: What does \"Donovan is seeing unusually high usage\" mean?\nA: It is the fair-use safety limit, which exists to stop runaway scripts. Ordinary use doesn't reach it. Email support@deepwelltechnology.com and we'll sort it out.\n\n## Using Donovan and reading sources [article_id: using-donovan-and-sources]\nDonovan is the DeepWell assistant that answers questions from your own records. This support chat explains how DeepWell works. Questions about your customers, equipment or jobs belong in Donovan.\nQ: What is Donovan?\nA: Donovan answers questions in plain language using your uploaded records: who a document is for, what an invoice totals, what a permit or agreement says, and, for equipment paperwork, warranty status, last service, model and serial. Every answer shows the source document, and if Donovan isn't sure it says so and shows the document instead of guessing.\nQ: How do I ask Donovan a question?\nA: Open **Ask** in the app, on desktop or in the phone app, and type the question the way you would ask a coworker, for example an address, a serial number, a name or a date. You get the answer with the source attached.\nQ: What kinds of questions can Donovan answer?\nA: Things like \"What did we pay Acme Supply in March?\", \"Show me the signed permit for 12 Main\" or \"When did we last service the unit at 3247 Elm?\" For equipment paperwork it also covers warranty status, model and serial numbers, and which units are expiring soon. It answers from your own records only, and says so when something isn't on file.\nQ: Can Donovan be wrong?\nA: Yes, AI answers can be incomplete or wrong. A misread serial, an old scan or a document that was never uploaded can all cause it. That's why every answer cites its source. Check the cited document before relying on an answer for a warranty claim, a safety decision or anything with financial consequences.\nQ: Why did Donovan say it couldn't find something?\nA: Usually the document hasn't been uploaded or finished processing, or the name, address or serial was read differently. Try the address or serial number, check the document's status in Inbox, and correct any flagged fields. If Donovan still misses something it should have found, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Can this chat look up my customer records?\nA: No. This chat only answers questions about DeepWell itself. For anything about your own customers, equipment, jobs or documents, ask **Donovan** in the app.\nQ: Does Donovan learn from my data or other customers' data?\nA: Your records stay under your own account and are never pooled with another company's. Under our AI providers' API terms your content isn't used to train their models. Your corrections make the system sharper. See the security article for details.\n\n## Security and privacy [article_id: security-and-privacy]\nDeepWell describes its real, current controls on the Security & Privacy page and in the Privacy Policy. This article does not round up: it lists what is not done yet, too.\nQ: Is my data secure?\nA: Yes. Your records are stored under your own company's account and kept separate from every other customer's, and the database enforces that separation on every query. Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, and files sit in private storage that opens only through short-lived links. DeepWell staff have no standing access to your account: your admin can grant **support access** for a set time and revoke it at any time, and every access is recorded in your own activity log.\nQ: Can DeepWell see our data or files?\nA: DeepWell staff have no standing access to your account. Your records live under your company's own account, and the database enforces that isolation for every query. Inside the product, staff can look at your account only through **support access** that your admin grants for a set time and can revoke at any time, or in an emergency that is always logged where your admin can see it. Every access is recorded in your own activity log. The two founders also administer the hosting, database and file-storage accounts.\nQ: Is my data isolated from other customers?\nA: Yes. Every document, customer record and answer is stored under your company's account and is never pooled with another customer's data. The database enforces this at the row level on every query, not only in application code.\nQ: Is my data encrypted?\nA: Data is encrypted in transit with HTTPS/TLS, and files and database records are encrypted at rest by our storage providers (Cloudflare and Neon). Per-tenant encryption keys are not implemented: each customer's data is isolated by the database, not by separate keys.\nQ: Is DeepWell SOC 2 certified or compliant?\nA: No. DeepWell has **no SOC 2 or equivalent certification** yet, and it hasn't had an independent third-party audit. The controls described on the Security & Privacy page are real, but I can't claim a certification. For a security questionnaire, email security@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Does DeepWell use my documents to train AI?\nA: No. To read documents and answer questions, DeepWell sends content and query text to its AI providers (Anthropic, and Voyage AI for search). Under those providers' API terms, that content is not used to train their models, and it is not shared with any other customer. AI answers can still be wrong, so check the citation.\nQ: Who are your subprocessors?\nA: Cloudflare R2 (file storage), Neon (database), Clerk (sign-in), Anthropic (AI reading and answering), Voyage AI (search), Inngest (background jobs, identifiers only), Vercel (hosting and cookieless analytics), Stripe (payments), Resend (email) and Sentry (scrubbed error monitoring). All are US-based. See the Privacy Policy for the full table.\nQ: Are files private?\nA: Yes. Uploaded files are not public. Each time a document is opened, DeepWell issues a short-lived signed link for that one file, so a leaked link can't be reused for long and a file can't be found by guessing a URL.\nQ: Does DeepWell use cookies or advertising trackers?\nA: No tracking or advertising cookies, and no cookie banner. The only cookies are strictly necessary sign-in cookies from our authentication provider. Site analytics are cookieless.\nQ: What if I find a security problem?\nA: Please tell us before anyone else: **security@deepwelltechnology.com**. We acknowledge real reports and work with you on a fix. There is no formal published breach-notification deadline yet. Our commitment is to notify affected account admins without undue delay after confirming a breach.\nQ: Where can I read the privacy policy or terms?\nA: They are at deepwelltechnology.com/privacy and deepwelltechnology.com/terms, with a plain-language security summary at deepwelltechnology.com/security. I can't give legal advice. For a contract or DPA question, email privacy@deepwelltechnology.com or support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## Support access grants [article_id: support-access-grants]\nQ: How does support access work?\nA: Our support team does not have standing access to your documents. When you want our help, for example troubleshooting an issue, you grant temporary support access from your account settings, and you can revoke it at any time.\nQ: Can I see what support looked at?\nA: Support has no standing access; access happens only under a grant you give. Every grant, and everything accessed under it, is recorded in your account's activity log, so there is a record of who looked at what, and when. Uploads, edits, exports and support access are all written to that log.\n\n## Deleting data and closing your account [article_id: data-export-and-deletion]\nQ: How do I delete a document?\nA: You can delete any document from your account at any time. Deletion removes it from both the file vault and the search index within our normal processing cycle.\nQ: How do I delete all my data or close my account?\nA: A company admin can export the company's data or delete it entirely, at any time, from **Team → Settings**, so you don't need to email us and wait. Deleting the company also cancels its subscription. You can also ask us at privacy@deepwelltechnology.com, and we will remove your company's account data and stored documents, except where we're required to keep limited records for legal or accounting reasons. If you want a person to handle it, I can send your request to the team.\nQ: What is kept after deletion?\nA: We remove your company's account data and stored documents, except where we're required to retain limited records for legal or accounting reasons. For specifics, email privacy@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: What happens to my data if I cancel?\nA: You may request an export or deletion after canceling. We may suspend an account for non-payment or a terms violation, and after termination you can request an export for a reasonable period before it is deleted. Export from Team → Settings while you still have access.\n\n## Contacting the DeepWell team [article_id: contacting-humans]\nReal people answer. Pick the address that matches your question.\nQ: How do I contact DeepWell?\nA: All addresses end in @deepwelltechnology.com. **hello@** for sales and demos, **support@** for help using DeepWell, **billing@** for invoices and charges, **privacy@** for privacy and data requests, and **security@** to report a security concern.\nQ: Can I talk to a real person?\nA: Yes. I can send your question to the team from this chat. Choose **Send to a person**, add your email and we'll reply by email. Or write to support@deepwelltechnology.com directly.\nQ: How fast will support respond?\nA: Response targets depend on the plan: Solo, email with a next-business-day response. Team, email and chat, same business day. Crew, email, chat and phone, 2 hours for urgent issues. Fleet, a named contact, 1 hour for urgent issues, 24/7. I can't make promises beyond those listed targets. Phone support is listed for Crew and Fleet, so email support@ to get set up.\nQ: How do I talk to sales or get a demo?\nA: Email hello@deepwelltechnology.com. The best first step is to send a sample box, and on the first call you ask real questions about your own business. Fleet pricing beyond the base is quoted by email.\nQ: Can I ask a question before I sign up?\nA: Yes. On the DeepWell website, the **Talk to us** section at the bottom of the home page has a short form: add your name, company and work email, say roughly how many documents you have and where they are, and type your question. Sterling and Hilton read every one and reply by email within one business day. You can also just email hello@deepwelltechnology.com.\nQ: Who will I work with during setup?\nA: Sterling Chapman works with you from your first sample through go-live. Hilton Chapman leads customer relationships. Fleet customers get a named contact. Crew includes a scheduled onboarding call.\nQ: I need help with something urgent\nA: Email support@deepwelltechnology.com with what you see and when it started. Urgent-issue response targets are listed for Crew (2 hours) and Fleet (1 hour, 24/7). I can also send it to the team from here. You can also check status.deepwelltechnology.com to see whether DeepWell is up right now.\nQ: Is there a status page?\nA: Yes. The public status page is at status.deepwelltechnology.com. It shows whether the website, the app, the phone app and records and answers are up right now, with a history of past incidents. An uptime SLA is **coming soon** and is not in place today, including the 99.5% uptime SLA on Fleet. If something looks down, email support@deepwelltechnology.com.\n\n## What is not available yet [article_id: known-limits-and-coming-soon]\nThese items are marked coming soon on the website, or are called out as not done in our security notes. I can't promise dates or that they will ship.\nQ: What features are coming soon?\nA: Nothing here has a date, and I can't promise one. Live today: ask donovan, phone app scanning, warranty tracking and export, bulk upload, records search, public status page, help chat. Marked **coming soon** on the site, being built next: email and folder upload, google drive sync, branch scoping, callback analytics, backups and per-company restore, uptime sla. Later, not available today: electrical, plumbing, property management, fleet and equipment rental.\nQ: Does DeepWell make backups?\nA: Daily off-site backups with a 30-day restore are marked coming soon on the Crew plan, and 6-hourly backups with per-company restore on Fleet. They aren't available as a feature today. Our database provider keeps its own point-in-time history, which ages out on its own retention window. You can export your data yourself any time.\nQ: What are the known security gaps?\nA: Openly: no SOC 2 or equivalent certification yet, no per-tenant encryption keys (isolation is enforced by the database), no formal published breach-notification deadline, and emergency support access is trust-based but always logged and visible to you. Bundling all original files into one zip export is not built yet either.\nQ: Is there a desktop or App Store app?\nA: DeepWell is a web app. On a computer, use deepwelltechnology.com/app. The phone app installs from your browser and isn't in an app store.\nQ: Can DeepWell check who is generating callbacks?\nA: Technician callback analytics are marked coming soon and are not available today.";
